From 4a67b0b6517cafae3a230c6951d8e068a2787839 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:33:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: no legacy bitmaps; unreachable resources removed

- 697 resource files removed: every layout, menu, drawable and bitmap
  nothing live reaches (the removed camera module's artwork, holo menus,
  sounds, preferences), plus their value entries; ids the code still names
  are declared in values/plait_ids.xml
- Every remaining UI bitmap replaced: the GL renderer's overlays (play,
  panorama, camera, album labels, undo, offline) use the design guide's
  icons (ResourceTexture and the label maker draw vectors via
  PlaitIcons); pressed/selected frames, the undo panel and popups are
  plain tints and shapes; menus and legacy layouts use ps_ icons; the
  video scrubber and trim handles, the crop/curve handle and the editor's
  spot mask are drawn in code; the editor's shadows are gone (tone, not
  shadows); the holo spinner and overscroll glow are replaced or off
- Left as bitmaps: image data only (Looks colour tables, frame textures,
  Markup brushes)
- versionCode 40060

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VXjYUWzBqMCeUoJD2Suc4
